"""Component layers.1.mlp.down_proj:1611 (Qwen3-1.7B, layer 1 MLP down-projection).

Mostly quiet (typical |activation| ~0.05); it has a few sharp, readable triggers:

1. HTML anchor tag name. The letter `a` that names an `<a>` tag (`<a href`, `</a>`, `><a`,
   `"><a`) is strongly negative (about -4 to -9). So is `a` in "Act a" (the journal "Acta").
   The one-token `<a` is about -4; a capital `A` after a tag opener is weaker, about -2.
2. "Title:" opening a document. The `:` right after a document-initial `Title` is +4.7.
   The same `:` mid-document is about 0.
3. The first token of a document, which the model sees with no left context, so its
   activation depends only on that token. Code-comment or preprocessor starts (`#`, `//`,
   `/*`, `--`) are mildly positive (+0.5). Newlines, digits, bare capital letters and
   special tokens are mildly negative (-0.2 to -0.6). Bare lowercase words are about -0.15.
   Space-led words are about 0.

Everything else is predicted as 0. Measured on training rows, this captures the large
events; the diffuse remainder is not explained.
