"""Detect short EN-like written fragments, including E + N across tokens.

Romanization extends the same spelling rule to other scripts. Long words and
prefixes recognized as common English words get weaker responses. Cross-token
E + N is stronger, particularly in katakana; EN as a URL language code is also
strong. Numeric strengths were calibrated on training examples. This is not a
pronunciation model and does not account for all contextual variation.
