Opening digits and single spaces have weaker pulses than words. Longer
English tokens and punctuation clusters have stronger ones, as do words
about property, commerce, and organizations. Elsewhere this is quiet,
except for small positive signals on code member-access syntax.
Token-specific differences within these broad categories are not modeled.
